 60; Detect Ambush 30+10 = 40; Piloting one of choice +15 as a Pilot pick with bonus 15; Power Armor Combat: Elite -> the generic Robot Combat Elite (no Counterstrike elite row); W.P. Energy Rifle, W.P. Energy Pistol; Hand to Hand: Expert to Martial Arts for one other skill (costs martial_arts 1). || RELATED: seven, plus one at levels 3, 5, 7, 9 and 11; every category Any with the printed bonuses, Medical Paramedic only (+5%). Secondary: five, same limits without bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: Mark I body armor; ARP-1 or IAR-20; one energy weapon of choice as a choice of the Legion''s own human-sized arms (IAR-2 sidearm, ARP-1, IAR-20); 4 E-clips or magazines for each -> e-clip x8 with a note; survival knife; first aid kit. The ''field kit'' has no catalog row and is not stored; mission-issue extra gear is prose. The retired veterans'' substitute kit is a restriction line. || MONEY: 2000 credits a month and the book says the character starts with one month''s pay, so starting_money 2000 - the same reading as the coalition-grunt and coalition-technical-officer (fix-missing-starting-money.sql: ''starts off with one month''s pay''). The 800 credit combat hazard bonus is paid only in combat and is side_effects prose. || CYBERNETICS: ''see above'' - all as special_abilities; no bionics catalog block. Skill Note pointing to Rifts Japan is not stored."
